-- T0420
{id="t0420-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The route on the kitchen copy — a folded page",body="They told us the road was still open. The map pinned beside the shopping list had already been changed in pencil, and the neighbor who came for water said the gate was locked.\n\nI kept the older copy in a coat pocket while everyone else was told to use the new one. I had meant to save it only until someone could explain the difference. By then the ordinary work around us had stopped."},
{id="t0420-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A place under the names — a folded page",body="I counted everyone in the queue before I counted cars. The person carrying the list wrote down the cars first and ran out of room for the family walking behind them.\n\nThe youngest still asked whether the driver knew where we were. We compared what we had seen with what was written there. The second account omitted the small part that had frightened us."},
{id="t0420-03",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The second pickup time — a folded page",body="My brother stayed for the later vehicle because our aunt could not get into the first. Its time was written on the back of a lunch receipt. No driver at the next barrier knew of it.\n\nThe pencil count did not change when the people standing beside me did. I left the date on the page and did not try to straighten the damaged edge. Someone else might remember the same afternoon."},
{id="t0420-04",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Inside the crossed square — a folded page",body="The house was marked cleared while we were still packing. I put a square around the date on our own copy. We waited for someone to return and ask who was inside.\n\nThe person who had written the first directions could no longer be found. My family asked me to put the paper away with the bills. I kept it separate because the person involved might come back for it."},
{id="t0420-05",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A seat counted twice — a folded page",body="The woman at the gate read our names aloud and put us on a bus list. Another person came out with a new list and said the first bus had already taken us.\n\nI left room for a correction and carried the paper through the night. I had meant to save it only until someone could explain the difference. By then the ordinary work around us had stopped."},
{id="t0420-06",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The return line — a folded page",body="A man in a vest promised to come back after he moved the first group. His pencil left an unfinished arrow on my paper. I kept the page when the rest of the notices were pulled down.\n\nThe last vehicle passed with space for the supplies but none listed for us. We compared what we had seen with what was written there. The second account omitted the small part that had frightened us."},
{id="t0420-07",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="After the barrier moved — a folded page",body="We followed the directions given at dawn and found a chain across the road. Someone had moved the crossing but left the old sign standing. My father had memorized its distance because he could not read the smaller print.\n\nI kept the older copy in a coat pocket while everyone else was told to use the new one. I left the date on the page and did not try to straighten the damaged edge. Someone else might remember the same afternoon."},
{id="t0420-08",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A count made indoors — a folded page",body="The clerk counted the beds as if each held one person. My mother was sitting beside my sister, waiting for her to stand. On the posted total there was only one of them.\n\nThe youngest still asked whether the driver knew where we were. My family asked me to put the paper away with the bills. I kept it separate because the person involved might come back for it."},
{id="t0420-09",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The parcel that returned — a folded page",body="I sent a change of address with the driver who said he could cross. The parcel came back with the new address rubbed out. The note from my husband inside had never been opened.\n\nThe pencil count did not change when the people standing beside me did. I had meant to save it only until someone could explain the difference. By then the ordinary work around us had stopped."},
{id="t0420-10",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Two versions of the line — a folded page",body="I copied the first line because it included our street. The replacement left the street out but retained the same number of vehicles. We stood beside the mailbox until the engines were gone.\n\nThe person who had written the first directions could no longer be found. We compared what we had seen with what was written there. The second account omitted the small part that had frightened us."},
-- T0421
{id="t0421-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="A mark above the water — a folded page",body="The bottle looked clean until it dried, when a green line appeared above the water. We had filled it from the tap after the field truck sprayed the far rows, the ones with the new seed mix.\n\nThe dog would not drink from the dish left outside. I kept the bottle until someone could tell me what was in that spray."},
{id="t0421-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The garden after misting — a folded page",body="I covered the herbs when the trial vehicle passed. By evening the leaves under the cover had curled too. The neighbor said the spray could not have crossed the fence, but her laundry had the same pale grains.\n\nThe tomatoes along the fence went spotted within the week. I pressed one leaf in this page to compare against the next row."},
{id="t0421-03",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Supper from the wrong side — a folded page",body="The feed-store driver left a sack and stopped to wash his hands before accepting a cup of tea. He asked us not to use the rain barrel. The seed treatment on the sack was not mentioned on the delivery slip.\n\nThe next family along the road noticed the smell without seeing the truck. By week's end the beans watered from our barrel had gone yellow. I left the date on the page and did not straighten the damaged edge."},
{id="t0421-04",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Boots by the threshold — a folded page",body="The workers removed their boots outside. By morning the pale dust had traveled inside on the dog's paws. No one in the house had gone near the trial rows, yet the garden by the door was dusted white.\n\nI wrote down the day because the wilting started after it. I kept it separate from the bills because the person involved might come back for it."},
{id="t0421-05",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The jar in a grocery bag — a folded page",body="I was asked to keep this sample apart from the cooking jars. Its lid came loose on the way back from the orchard. The grocery bag was set on the table before I noticed the sweet chemical smell.\n\nThe child's blanket was drying nearby and held the same fine dust. The potted peppers on the sill curled the next morning. I had meant to save it only until someone could explain the difference."},
{id="t0421-06",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="A fence too late — a folded page",body="They painted the boundary posts after the field test was done. The path we use for water lies beyond the last post. We had walked it that morning with the children, past rows still wet with spray.\n\nWe washed the small cup twice and put it away from the others. The wet rows were stunted by the next week; the dry ones beside them were not."},
{id="t0421-07",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The calf’s water pail — a folded page",body="The calves refused their water before the county car appeared. I poured it into a spare pail and found an oily rim when it settled. We had drawn it from the same shallow well as ours.\n\nThe dog would no longer drink from the dish left outside. I left the date on the page and did not try to straighten the damaged edge. Someone else might remember the same afternoon."},
{id="t0421-08",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="A wash after the shift — a folded page",body="The driver washed the sprayer beside the feed shop. He paid for soap but not for another bucket. The rinse water ran through the drain toward gardens downhill, and the beds there showed bleached leaf edges by the weekend.\n\nI kept the paper separate from the bills because the person involved might come back for it."},
{id="t0421-09",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="First rain on the roof — a folded page",body="The first rain after the field treatment left yellow flecks in a pan under the leak. We had shut the window before the truck came. I saved the pan because no one believed me when I described it.\n\nThe next family along the road noticed the smell without seeing the truck. I had meant to save it only until someone could explain the difference. By then the ordinary work around us had stopped."},
{id="t0421-10",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="A receipt from the seed counter — a folded page",body="The receipt includes a small charge for sample jars. The shopkeeper wrote a household address beside it, not a field number. I asked why, and he said the delivery men used whatever route remained open.\n\nI wrote down the day because the first warning arrived after it. We compared what we had seen with what was written there. The second account omitted the small part that had frightened us."},
-- T0422
