{id="t0422-04",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Inside the crossed square — kept overnight",body="The house was marked cleared while we were still packing. I put a square around the date on our own copy. We waited for someone to return and ask who was inside.\n\nThe last vehicle passed with space for the supplies but none listed for us. I had meant to save it only until someone could explain the difference. By then the ordinary work around us had stopped."},
{id="t0422-05",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A seat counted twice — kept overnight",body="The woman at the gate read our names aloud and put us on a bus list. Another person came out with a new list and said the first bus had already taken us.\n\nI kept the older copy in a coat pocket while everyone else was told to use the new one. We compared what we had seen with what was written there. The second account omitted the small part that had frightened us."},
{id="t0422-06",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The return line — kept overnight",body="A man in a vest promised to come back after he moved the first group. His pencil left an unfinished arrow on my paper. I kept the page when the rest of the notices were pulled down.\n\nThe youngest still asked whether the driver knew where we were. I left the date on the page and did not try to straighten the damaged edge. Someone else might remember the same afternoon."},
{id="t0422-07",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="After the barrier moved — kept overnight",body="We followed the directions given at dawn and found a chain across the road. Someone had moved the crossing but left the old sign standing. My father had memorized its distance because he could not read the smaller print.\n\nThe pencil count did not change when the people standing beside me did. My family asked me to put the paper away with the bills. I kept it separate because the person involved might come back for it."},
{id="t0422-08",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A count made indoors — kept overnight",body="The clerk counted the beds as if each held one person. My mother was sitting beside my sister, waiting for her to stand. On the posted total there was only one of them.\n\nThe person who had written the first directions could no longer be found. I had meant to save it only until someone could explain the difference. By then the ordinary work around us had stopped."},
{id="t0422-09",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The parcel that returned — kept overnight",body="I sent a change of address with the driver who said he could cross. The parcel came back with the new address rubbed out. The note from my husband inside had never been opened.\n\nI left room for a correction and carried the paper through the night. We compared what we had seen with what was written there. The second account omitted the small part that had frightened us."},
{id="t0422-10",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Two versions of the line — kept overnight",body="I copied the first line because it included our street. The replacement left the street out but retained the same number of vehicles. We stood beside the mailbox until the engines were gone.\n\nThe last vehicle passed with space for the supplies but none listed for us. I left the date on the page and did not try to straighten the damaged edge. Someone else might remember the same afternoon."},
-- T0423
{id="t0423-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="A mark above the water — kept overnight",body="The bottle looked clean until it dried, when a green line appeared above the water. We had filled it after the field truck passed, at a tap on the other side of the road.\n\nThe next family along the road noticed the smell without seeing the truck. The bean leaves watered from that tap had turned dark and slick. I kept the bottle overnight to see if the line came back."},
{id="t0423-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The garden after misting — kept overnight",body="I covered the herbs when the trial vehicle passed. By evening the leaves under the cover had curled too. The neighbor said the spray could not have crossed the fence, but her laundry had the same pale grains.\n\nI wrote down the day because the leaves started to curl after it. The lettuce beside the fence bolted early. Someone else might remember the same afternoon."},
{id="t0423-03",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Supper from the wrong side — kept overnight",body="The feed-store driver left a sack and stopped to wash his hands before accepting a cup of tea. He asked us not to use the rain barrel. The seed treatment on the sack was not mentioned on the delivery slip.\n\nThe child's blanket was drying nearby and held the same fine dust. The treated seed had already been sown along our fence. I kept this separate because the person involved might come back for it."},
{id="t0423-04",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Boots by the threshold — kept overnight",body="The workers removed their boots outside. By morning the pale dust had traveled inside on the dog’s paws. No one in the house had gone near the trial rows.\n\nWe washed the small cup twice and put it away from the others. I had meant to save it only until someone could explain the difference. By then the ordinary work around us had stopped."},
{id="t0423-05",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The jar in a grocery bag — kept overnight",body="The sprayed rows by the orchard were still wet when I filled the sample jar. Its lid came loose in the grocery bag, and the table smelled of that bitter spray all evening.\n\nThe dog would not drink from the dish left outside. The pear leaves along the sprayed rows curled and went brown within two days."},
{id="t0423-06",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The wind over the bean rows — kept overnight",body="We sprayed the lower field after the seed trial and the wind carried it over the water path. The bean rows beside the path are scorched in a long yellow streak.\n\nI left the date on the page and did not smooth the torn edge. The leaves on the nearest rows are still curling."},
{id="t0423-07",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The calf’s water pail — kept overnight",body="The calves refused their water. I poured it into a spare pail and found an oily rim once it settled, the same sheen as the puddles in the sprayed pasture. We draw from the same shallow well as the field.\n\nThe oats along that pasture have gone patchy and pale. I kept the pail aside from the others."},
{id="t0423-08",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="A wash after the shift — kept overnight",body="The driver washed the sprayer beside the closed shop. He paid for soap but not for another bucket. The water ran through the drain toward houses that had no notice about the trial.\n\nI wrote down the day because the first warning arrived after it. I had meant to save it only until someone could explain the difference. By then the ordinary work around us had stopped."},
{id="t0423-09",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="First rain on the roof — kept overnight",body="The first rain after the field treatment left yellow flecks in a pan under the leak. The same flecks lay on the wheat leaves outside, thick along the rows we sprayed.\n\nThe child's blanket was drying nearby and held the same fine dust. I saved the pan because no one believed me when I described it."},
{id="t0423-10",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="A receipt from the seed counter — kept overnight",body="The seed counter receipt lists a small charge for sample jars and a bag of the new treated seed. The corn I planted from it came up stunted and grey-streaked, while the old seed in the next row stands green.\n\nWe washed the small cup twice and put it away from the others. I wrote down the planting day beside the receipt."},
-- T0424
{id="t0424-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The route on the kitchen copy — in the margin",body="They told us the road was still open. The map pinned beside the shopping list had already been changed in pencil, and the neighbor who came for water said the gate was locked.\n\nI left room for a correction and carried the paper through the night. I left the date on the page and did not try to straighten the damaged edge. Someone else might remember the same afternoon."},
{id="t0424-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A place under the names — in the margin",body="I counted everyone in the queue before I counted cars. The person carrying the list wrote down the cars first and ran out of room for the family walking behind them.\n\nThe last vehicle passed with space for the supplies but none listed for us. My family asked me to put the paper away with the bills. I kept it separate because the person involved might come back for it."},
{id="t0424-03",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The second pickup time — in the margin",body="My brother stayed for the later vehicle because our aunt could not get into the first. Its time was written on the back of a lunch receipt. No driver at the next barrier knew of it.\n\nI kept the older copy in a coat pocket while everyone else was told to use the new one. I had meant to save it only until someone could explain the difference. By then the ordinary work around us had stopped."},
