{id="t0425-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The garden after misting — in the margin",body="I covered the herbs when the trial vehicle passed. By evening the leaves under the cover had curled too. The neighbor said the spray could not have crossed the fence, but her laundry had the same pale grains.\n\nWe washed the small cup twice and put it away from the others. My family asked me to put the paper away with the bills. I kept it separate because the person involved might come back for it."},
{id="t0425-03",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Supper from the wrong side — in the margin",body="The feed-store driver left a sack of the new treated grain and washed his hands before accepting a cup of tea. He said the sack dust burned. The delivery slip said nothing of it.\n\nThe dog would not drink from the dish left outside. The barley I sowed from that sack came up thin and spotted, row after row."},
{id="t0425-04",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Boots by the threshold — in the margin",body="The workers took their boots off outside after the spraying. By morning the pale dust had still traveled inside on the dog's paws. No one in the house had gone near the sprayed rows.\n\nThe lettuce bed by the door has gone limp where the dog crossed it. I set the page beside the boots."},
{id="t0425-05",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The jar in a grocery bag — in the margin",body="I was asked to keep this sample apart from the cooking jars. Its lid came loose on the way back from the orchard. The grocery bag was set on the table before I noticed the smell.\n\nThe next family along the road noticed the smell without seeing the truck. I left the date on the page and did not try to straighten the damaged edge. Someone else might remember the same afternoon."},
{id="t0425-06",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The wind over the squash rows — in the margin",body="We sprayed the lower field after the seed trial. The water path runs beside it, and the wind carried the mist across. The squash along that path has blackened leaves in a long streak.\n\nI wrote down the day because the leaves turned afterward. I kept the page separate from the bills."},
{id="t0425-07",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The calf’s water pail — in the margin",body="The calves refused their water before the county car appeared. I poured it into a spare pail and found an oily rim when it settled. We had drawn it from the same shallow well as ours.\n\nThe child’s blanket was drying nearby and held the same fine dust. I had meant to save it only until someone could explain the difference. By then the ordinary work around us had stopped."},
{id="t0425-08",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="A wash after the shift — in the margin",body="The driver washed the spray rig beside the feed shop. The rinse ran down the drain toward the vegetable plots behind the houses, and by the next week the cabbages there had yellowed in a fan shape.\n\nWe washed the small cup twice and put it away from the others. I noted the cabbage rows on the page."},
{id="t0425-09",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="First rain on the roof — in the margin",body="The first rain after the field treatment left yellow flecks in a pan under the leak. The same flecks sit on the wheat leaves, thick along the rows we sprayed and absent where we did not.\n\nThe dog would not drink from the dish left outside. I saved the pan because no one believed me when I described it."},
{id="t0425-10",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="A receipt from the seed counter — in the margin",body="The seed counter receipt lists a small charge for sample jars and a sack of the new treated seed. The shopkeeper wrote a field number beside it. The corn from that sack came up grey-streaked and stunted.\n\nI kept the receipt with my planting notes so I could compare the rows."},
